---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import { getImage, Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SocialIcons from "../components/SocialIcons.astro";
import { FaCalendar } from "react-icons/fa";
import { formatDate } from "../utils/formatDate";
import avatarLargeImage from "../assets/avatar-large.jpeg";

// Get posts with "popular" tag, sorted by date, limit to 5
const allPosts = await getCollection("posts");
const popularPosts = allPosts
  .filter((post) => post.data.tags && post.data.tags.includes("popular"))
  .map((post) => {
    // Extract date from post id (YYYY-MM-DD--slug format)
    const dateMatch = post.id.match(/^([0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2})--/);
    const date = dateMatch ? dateMatch[1] : post.data.date || "";

    // Extract slug
    const slug = post.id
      .replace(/^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}--/, "")
      .replace(/\/index\.(md|mdx)$/, "");

    return {
      ...post,
      date,
      slug,
    };
  })
  .sort((a, b) => b.date.localeCompare(a.date))
  .slice(0, 5);

// Generate optimized cover images for popular posts
const popularPostsWithCovers = await Promise.all(
  popularPosts.map(async (post) => {
    if (!post.data.cover) return { ...post, coverImage: null };

    const coverImage = await getImage({
      src: post.data.cover,
      width: 400,
      format: "webp",
    });

    return { ...post, coverImage };
  })
);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Jade Rubick builds humane, effective engineering organizations. His background, what he believes, and what he writes."
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <div class="about-header">
      <Image
        src={avatarLargeImage}
        alt="Jade Rubick"
        class="avatar"
        widths={[800, 1200, 1600]}
        sizes="(max-width: 799px) 800px, (max-width: 1199px) 1200px, 1600px"
      />
    </div>

    <section class="about-content">
      <h2>Hello</h2>

      <p>
        My name is Jade Rubick. I build thriving engineering organizations. My
        specialty is humane, results-focused organizations.
      </p>

      <h2>Background</h2>

      <p>
        I started out as a developer and have spent most of my career leading
        engineering teams. I was a VP of Engineering at New Relic, where I wrote
        the product handbook that described how our product teams worked. I led
        engineering and product at Gremlin and Campus, and was CTO at Flatfile.
      </p>

      <p>
        Since 2020, I've stepped into engineering leadership roles at startups
        like Mode, Castle, RevolutionParts, and SimpleConsign, usually to
        stabilize the organization, improve how it delivers, and then hire my
        permanent replacement. Doing that over and over has taught me a lot
        about how engineering organizations work, how they fail, and what it
        takes to hire the right leader for them.
      </p>

      <p>
        These days most of my time goes to advising CTOs, VPs of Engineering,
        and CEOs at startups.
      </p>

      <h2>What I believe</h2>

      <p>
        I don't think you have to choose between effective and humane. The
        organizations I most admire ship well <em>because</em> they treat people
        well: people know what's expected of them, can see why their work
        matters, and are trusted to figure out how to do it.
      </p>

      <p>
        I treat organizational changes as experiments. Explain the reasoning,
        try the change, see what happens, and keep or roll it back. Most of the
        time the lightweight fix beats the heavy one.
      </p>

      <p>
        Underrepresented people are the best test of a company's culture.
        Improvements you make for them usually make the company better for
        everyone. At New Relic, we achieved an employee NPS that was equal across
        demographic groups. At Gremlin, underrepresented representation in
        engineering went from 7% to 38% in a little over a year. What helped was
        engineering levels, fair compensation, a good promotion process, and a
        humane hiring process.
      </p>

      <h2>What I write, and why</h2>

      <p>
        I like to share what I've learned. Most leadership advice is either
        simplistic or too abstract to use, and I try to write the practical,
        specific version I wished I'd had.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="/newsletter/">Engineering Leadership Weekly</a>: one essay a
          week on building humane, effective engineering organizations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/decoding-leadership/">Decoding Leadership</a>: a podcast
          where we break down the elements of humane and effective leadership.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/course/">A course for new managers</a>, delivered by email
          over five months.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/wiki/">The wiki</a>: my working notes on engineering
          leadership topics.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Working together</h2>

      <p>
        If you lead an engineering organization and want an experienced partner,
        see <a href="/work-with-me/">how I work with clients</a>. Or just{" "}
        <a href="/contact/">say hello</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Most popular posts</h2>

      <div class="popular-posts">
        {
          popularPostsWithCovers.map((post) => (
            <article class="post-item">
              {post.coverImage && (
                <a href={`/${post.slug}/`} class="post-image-link">
                  {/* Deep below the fold here, so these stay lazy —
                      `attributes` already sets it; no need to repeat it. */}
                  <img
                    src={post.coverImage.src}
                    alt={post.data.title}
                    {...post.coverImage.attributes}
                    class="post-image"
                  />
                </a>
              )}
              <div class="post-content">
                <h3>
                  <a href={`/${post.slug}/`}>{post.data.title}</a>
                </h3>
                <div class="post-meta">
                  <span class="post-date">
                    <FaCalendar size={14} /> {formatDate(post.date)}
                  </span>
                </div>
                {post.data.tags && post.data.tags.length > 0 && (
                  <div class="post-tags">
                    {post.data.tags.map((tag) => (
                      <a href={`/tags/${tag}/`} class="tag-chip">
                        #{tag}
                      </a>
                    ))}
                  </div>
                )}
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <p class="github-note">
        This blog's code is open sourced on <a
          href="https://www.github.com/jadeforrest/blog/">GitHub</a
        > thanks to <a href="https://github.com/baobabKoodaa/blog"
          >Atte Juvonen</a
        > and others before him. Feel free to submit corrections or use the code
        to create your own blog (but do not host my content elsewhere).
      </p>

      <div class="social-icons-container">
        <SocialIcons />
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .about-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-l);
  }

  .avatar {
    border-radius: 50%;
    width: 250px;
    height: 250px;
    object-fit: cover;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  }

  .about-content {
    font-size: 1.05em;
    line-height: var(--text-line-height-default);
  }

  .about-content h2 {
    font-size: var(--heading-size-h2);
    line-height: var(--heading-line-height-h2);
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
    color: var(--text-color-primary);
  }

  .about-content h3 {
    font-size: var(--heading-size-h3);
    line-height: var(--heading-line-height-h3);
    margin-top: var(--space-m);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
    color: var(--text-color-primary);
  }

  .about-content p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
  }

  .about-content a {
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .about-content a:hover {
    color: var(--color-brand-hover);
  }

  .about-content ul,
  .about-content ol {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
    padding-left: var(--space-l);
  }

  .about-content li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }

  .popular-posts {
    margin: var(--space-l) 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-s);
  }

  .post-item {
    display: flex;
    border-radius: var(--size-radius-default);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-neutral-white);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    transition: all var(--time-duration-default);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
  }

  .post-item:hover {
    box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
  }

  .post-image-link {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 200px;
    height: 150px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .post-image {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  .post-item:hover .post-image {
    transform: scale(1.05);
  }

  .post-content {
    flex: 1;
    padding: var(--space-m);
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .post-content h3 {
    font-size: var(--heading-size-h3);
    line-height: var(--heading-line-height-h3);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs) 0;
  }

  .post-content h3 a {
    color: var(--text-color-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .post-content h3 a:hover {
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
  }

  .post-meta {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-neutral-gray-j);
  }

  .post-date {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .post-date :global(svg) {
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
  }

  .post-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin-top: var(--space-s);
  }

  .tag-chip {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    background-color: var(--background-color-alt);
    border-radius: var(--size-radius-small);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .tag-chip:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    color: var(--color-neutral-white);
  }

  .github-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
    padding-top: var(--space-m);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--background-color-alt);
    font-size: var(--font-size-s);
  }

  .social-icons-container {
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .social-icons-container :global(.social-icons-wrapper) {
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .social-icons-container :global(.icons) {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-m);
    font-size: 40px;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .social-icons-container :global(.icons a) {
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .social-icons-container :global(.icons a:hover) {
    color: var(--color-brand-hover);
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }

  .social-icons-container :global(.icons svg) {
    width: 1em;
    height: 1em;
    fill: currentColor;
  }

  @media (max-width: 599px) {
    .avatar {
      width: 180px;
      height: 180px;
    }

    .social-icons-container :global(.icons) {
      font-size: 32px;
    }

    .post-image-link {
      width: 120px;
      height: 90px;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .about-content {
      padding: 0 var(--space-m);
    }

    .post-item {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
    }
  }
</style>
